# The in-flight journal (PLAN.md 1.4). Machine state, not history:
# what it holds is only meaningful to the run that wrote it.
.devoid-journal.json

# ⚠️ THE README TELLS YOU TO CREATE THIS. Following the install instructions wrote
# an untracked file into a clean clone and left it dirty; the path inside it is
# specific to one machine, so it must never be committed either.
devoid.config.json
.devoid-journal.json.lock
.devoid-journal.json.tmp
.claude/worktrees/

# Brand source art. The eight FINALS at the top level are tracked -- the icon,
# the two wordmarks, the three banners and the nebula are what anything else
# gets rebuilt from. Every SUBFOLDER is ignored: the PSDs are 59 MB of the
# 157 MB total, and the WIP renders are exploration, not source. Harkirat's
# call 2026-09-05. The trailing `/` matches directories only, so a new WIP
# folder is ignored the day it appears without anyone remembering to add it.
DEVOID Logo Assets/*/

# Your work history (PLAN.md 5.1). Per-machine, not shared: every real render
# appends a row carrying local absolute paths, so tracking it dirties the tree
# on every use and makes two branches conflict on a merge that means nothing.
# ⚠️ labels/protection.jsonl is the OPPOSITE case and STAYS TRACKED -- that log
# is evidence, meant to accumulate, and is pointed at from the engine repo.
jobs.jsonl

# the UI gate runs the server against a scratch data dir so it can never write
# to labels/protection.jsonl, which is tracked evidence
local/gate-data/

# measurement scratch — real files copied under distinct names, and its own data dir
local/scale-corpus/
local/scale-data/
local/scale-shots/
